@startuml
title Backend Architecture - r-products

actor "User / Client" as Client

package "Edge" {
  [Browser / Mobile App] as Frontend
  [CDN / Static Hosting] as CDN
}

package "Ingress" {
  [Load Balancer / NGINX] as LB
  [API Gateway] as Gateway
}

package "Application" {
  rectangle "Django REST API" as API
  rectangle "Auth (JWT)" as Auth
  rectangle "Product Service" as ProductSvc
  rectangle "Order Service" as OrderSvc
  rectangle "Admin / Management" as Admin
  rectangle "Celery Workers" as Workers
}

package "Integration & Storage" {
  database "PostgreSQL (prod) / SQLite (dev)" as DB
  cloud "Redis (cache & Celery broker)" as Redis
  storage "S3 / MinIO (media)" as S3
  [Payment Gateway] as PG
  [Email/SMS Provider] as ES
  [Monitoring / Metrics (Prometheus, Grafana)] as Monitor
}

Client --> Frontend : UI requests
Frontend --> CDN : static assets
Frontend --> Gateway : API requests (HTTPS)
Gateway --> LB
LB --> API : forward
API --> Auth : authenticate/authorize
API --> ProductSvc : product/catalog APIs
API --> OrderSvc : order & payment APIs
API --> DB : read/write
API --> Redis : cache, rate-limit
API --> S3 : upload/download media
OrderSvc --> PG : initiate payment
OrderSvc --> Workers : enqueue background tasks
Workers --> ES : send email/sms
Workers --> DB : write logs / update
Workers --> Redis : caching / task state
API --> Monitor : metrics / traces

note right of API
  - Containerized (Docker)
  - Scaled horizontally behind LB
  - Environment variables for secrets
end note

@enduml
